<h2 id="refuses">13. Things the code refuses to do</h2>
<div class="grid2">
<div><h4>Never launches on its own</h4><ul><li>Any second <code>start</code> on a started run</li><li>A relaunch when a receipt exists, even if the session is gone</li><li>A launch during <code>retry</code> or <code>reconcile</code></li><li>Anything without <code>--live</code></li></ul></div>
<div><h4>Never trusts worker claims</h4><ul><li>Changed-file lists come from Git, not the handoff</li><li>Checks are executed by the verifier in a fresh worktree</li><li>Missing or unparsable test output is "no evidence", not a pass</li><li>Packets and artifacts are re-hashed on every read</li></ul></div>
<div><h4>Never mutates frozen evidence</h4><ul><li>Existing lane packets are reused, not rerun</li><li>Policy or plan changes make the run unusable</li><li>An approved bundle cannot absorb new code; start a new run</li></ul></div>
<div><h4>Never reaches past the machine</h4><ul><li>No push, no PR, no branch deletion, no worktree cleanup</li><li>Integration is a local <code>--ff-only</code> after three explicit gates</li><li>No provider or billing fallback when usage runs out</li></ul></div>
